WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.067
-Guys, today is Friday,
and that's usually when

00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:04.267
I catch up on
some personal stuff.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:05.667
I check my in-box,
I return some e-mails,

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:07.467
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:00:07.467 --> 00:00:09.167
And I was running
a bit behind, so I thought --

00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:11.567
Yeah, thank you, sir or ma'am.

00:00:11.567 --> 00:00:12.801
If you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.367
can I write out some
thank-you notes right now?

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.167
I appreciate that.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:19.267
James, can I get some

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.734
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.734
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:27.033
Wow.
-Wow!

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.734
-Looks like he's in a good mood.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.734 --> 00:00:30.000
-He's in a good mood tonight.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:32.734
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.801
Thank you, this week, for giving
us 70-degree weather one day,

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.701
30 degrees the next,

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.934
and blacking out at 5:00 p.m.

00:00:39.934 --> 00:00:41.968
Mother nature, you're drunk.
Go to bed.

00:00:41.968 --> 00:00:43.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.567
Go off.

00:00:45.567 --> 00:00:46.901
Come on.

00:00:49.868 --> 00:00:50.901
-Alright.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.000
[ Soft music playing ]

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.767
Thank you, wool scarves,

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:57.834
for giving everyone
resting itch face.

00:00:57.834 --> 00:00:59.534
-Nice!

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:04.868
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:04.868 --> 00:01:07.400
-Thank you,
Space Force uniforms,

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.968
for making service members
look very prepared to protect

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:11.734
an FAO Schwarz.

00:01:11.734 --> 00:01:13.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.367
-Come on!

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.534
Poor Space Forcers.

00:01:19.534 --> 00:01:21.033
-Well, there's no
Space Force veterans.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.601
-Yeah, no. Exactly.

00:01:22.601 --> 00:01:23.934
-So we can --
-Come on.

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.634
-Yeah, we're gonna --
-They're called space cadets!

00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:27.901
-Yes.
-Thank you.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:30.601
Space cadets.

00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:31.868
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:31.868 --> 00:01:34.667
-Thank you, standing desks,
for being a great way to

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:37.234
stay fit at work
for three weeks until you go,

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.167
"Hey, does anyone
want this standing desk?

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.934
I'm not gonna do this.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.701
Back is killing me."

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.701
-And a ball?

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:47.801
[ Soft music playing ]

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.167
-Thank you, salad tongs,
for looking like

00:01:50.167 --> 00:01:53.801
a spoon, a fork, and a pair of
scissors are in a throuple.

00:01:55.267 --> 00:01:56.734
-Throuple.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:01.501
[ Soft music playing ]

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.968
-Thank you,
Captain America Chris Evans,

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.601
for being named
"People's" Sexiest Man Alive.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:10.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.100
I'm happy for you, but come on,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.634
you're not even the best-looking
captain in this room.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.567
Come on!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:17.801
There you have it.
Those were my thank-you notes.

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:19.100
We'll be right back with

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.968
"Freestylin' with The Roots,"
everybody. Come on.

